# Agent Checkpoint (Cursor)

Use the `acp` CLI for work memory. Do not invent storage formats.

## Triggers

- User asks to checkpoint / save progress / resume / 保存进度
- Before summarizing away details, clearing chat, or switching to another tool
- After important design decisions (record why + rejected options)
- Returning to a project after time away: `acp memory` then `acp resume`

## Commands

```bash
acp init
acp checkpoint --tool cursor --goal "..." --task "..." --decision "choice|why|rejected" --next "..."
acp checkpoint --task "..." --next "..."   # incremental
acp resume
acp resume --copy
acp memory
acp list
```

Paste `acp resume` output into a new chat to continue. Honor decisions and constraints; do not redo completed tasks.
